Well, after ascending for the first time, only a 5 weeks since I
started up nethack, I decided to post the story. I started Vara the
Chaotic Elven Wizard and thanks to reading basically every spoiler out
there, some early luck, only 1 or 2 major mistakes and a healthy dose
of overcautiousness, managed to ascend her to demigoddesshood.

I started out with knock, force bolt, slow digestion and I forget the
other. Ran into a bookstore and a huge potion shop on 3 and 4, went
into the mines, lucked into a ring of conflict on my way down,
descended down to Minetown, having my pet dog both steal for me and do
most of the killing on these first stages, and ended up with a few
other helpful spells early on (light, fireball).

Got to minetown, temple was lawful (and me being quite inexperienced
sofar) decided that I'd try and convert it with a convenient nearby
neutral unicorn bolt'd to death in a corridor. Wasn't instakilled when
the temple was converted, ran away, put conflict on and locked myself
in a room (didn't know that conflict required line of sight). When I
came back out, my pet was dead and the priest was still angry. I had
zapped myself with a wand of speed monster coming down to minetown, so
I decided to keep shooting down the priest on the run around the edges
of minetown. Eventually killed him. (This incident I call mistake #1).
I further check the shops, get myself a magic lamp, bless some water
on my new altar and summon forth a genie who kindly grants my wish for
+2 blessed GDSM. My god also decides I'm nice enough and gives me
Magicbane.

I head out of the mines, and decide to try Sokoban. Puzzles weren't
too hard, only broke 2-3 rocks because enemies got stuck behind them.
At some point I got a wand of fire, burned Elbereth outside the zoo
and just kept shooting. And the prize is... Reflection. Never took it
off the rest of the run. I burn Elbereth in the first floor of Sokoban
and start leaving the first bits of my stash.

I go back, finish the Mines and end up with the wine cellar, but find
a BoH on my way down... it really was a bunch of luck at the start of
the run. From here, I go back up and spend a long time just putzing
around slowly descending until I hit Medusa's. There's a titan by the
stairs who summons, and I run back up, realizing I need to get some
better protection before coming back. I end up doing the quest, which
was fairly easy, even though it was my first time getting past
Minetown. I hadn't found much in the way of better armor though, and
hadn't done protection buying yet (nor thought of it). I do however,
realize that conflict will likely disrupt that crowd I left at
Medusa's, so I equip it, go down and it works. I dig down a floor, pop
back up with a blindfold on and whack her to death. Perseus only has a
plain sack.

At this point I branchport back to my stash to leave a few things, and
on my way back I notice that there was one Vault left I hadn't gotten
to, so I dig into it, and sure enough, it's Ludios. I use conflict,
fireball and Elbereth to handle most of it. I walk around, use force
bolt to open the door, zap from afar with fireball till Croseus & Co
are dead, and use a wand of cold to walk the square over. I burn an
Elbereth, leave what's not the absolute essentials, and branchport to
my stash with 75 k total sitting there now. Only one problem, I killed
one of two aligned priests I could #chat to in the whole game. None
were generated between Minetown and Valley of the Dead.

So I decide to take my chances with the Castle (having a good coverage
of the basic resistances from corpses already). Conflict and fireball
win the day, and a 0:2 /oW I think hard and wish for Helm of
Brilliance, Gauntlets of Dexterity, recharge to 1:3 with a blessed
scroll of charging I had, then wish for Speed Boots, and 2 Magic
Markers. I write myself spellbooks of identify and polymorph and 12 or
so scrolls of enchant armor. So now I'm sitting at -37 AC, stats other
than charisma maxed after polypiling for potions of ability. I
polypile a bit with some scrolls I have left and eventually get 4
scrolls of genocide. Bye, liches, mind flayers and disenchanters/rust
monsters, and HELLLOOO NURSE! I nurse dance to ~200 HP and polypile
for more markers. No such luck. I polypile my rings, and get
everything I need, save levitate. So I wrest my last wish and ask for
it instead.

I grab the 75k in my stash and head down to the Valley of the Dead.
Clear it out and reduce my AC to -46 with the only priest left to me.
I continue down a few levels, dig Juiblex, and keep going down. I run
into Asmodeus and this is where things get hairy. I thought I had
killed him, but no such luck. So I descended again and this time got
Baalzebub. He's getting annoying, and on my way running back to the
stairs to trap him in, I fall down a trap door through two floors. Go
up again, and I'm standing next to Orcus. I chase him over to the
stairs, but he slips up before I can keep him there. So now Baalzebub
and Orcus are on one floor and Asmodeus is one above that. So I go up
and get to the upstair. They summon in Demogorgon and Yeenoghu. I
don't have Elbereth on the stair yet. So I go up it and Baalzebub
follows me. I descend, burn Elbereth and whack Demo, Yeeno and Orcus
to death. I got down to 30 HP at one point when I kept having to go
between unihorn and my spell of extra healing. After Demo went down
the rest was easy enough. I go back up a floor, get to the stairs
before Asmo and Baal, engrave with
Magicbane and whack them to death.

I go down to Vlad, grab the menorah and branchport to my stash. I
polypile for extra healing potions and some geno scrolls, nurse dance
myself to 350 HP, and take my out 7 candles from minetown. I go to an
altar, sacrifice the proper unicorn and start creating monster until I
end up crowned and get finger of death, which I had been sorely
lacking. At this point, the only critical spell I lacked was cure
sickness.

I head back down, making myself a decently quick path for going back
up, mark the vibrating square, drop my pickaxe since I have plenty of
wands of digging (this later factors into mistake #2), plus the spell
and start heading to Rodney. Finger of death is at 0% failure, so he's
a cakewalk. Try polying some of the spellbooks for curse sickness, but
no luck. I head down, perform the ritual, wade through the crowds and
grab the Amulet. Going up is easy, Rodney pops up 4 random times,
finger of death works each time. I get to my stash, and as I'm walking
to it, a giant throws a boulder on top of it. Not a problem, you
think, I'll just push it out of the way... yeah... the stash was in a
corner. I'll just wand it... wand of digging fails in Sokoban. I'll
use the spell! Same deal. I polypile my last uneeded tools for a
pickaxe... no luck. So I run back to the mines and grab the first
pickaxe I see. On my way back to the stash, I see one more spellbook
in a shop. So I poly it a few times and end up with cure sickness. Ah,
now I feel good about the planes.

I get the boulder off my stash, grab a few random scrolls, and
polypile till I have 4 scrolls of gold detection. I leave behind the
Dungeons of Doom and step onto the planes. Oh! Hi, Rodney, have a
finger. First portal is within 10 squares, and I waltz next to it with
2 zaps of digging. I prepare with conflict and levitate and waltz
through air, fire and water. I forget to remove conflict. Death is
next to me within about 15 moves. I'm down 60 max HP to 290. It's turn
and run time. I try the center Altar. Nope, neutral and famine, who
likes wands/fingers of death. I try the right altar, nope, lawful and
pestilence, who never touches me thanks to wand/finger of death. So
it's death at the left. Oh, wait, magic missile, duh. I zap him 3-4
times, step over his temporarily more dead than usual body, wade
through some priests and #offer the Amulet.

WYWYPI?
Why yes, yes, I do.

